{
 "description": "Paths the renderer must survive and draw as Chrome does: fills and strokes with finite coordinates as large as 1e30 (bounds past the i32 range, which Skia's safeRoundOut pins to +-(2^31-1)>>2), and dash lists that would cut more than 1,000,000 dashes (SkDashPath gives up and the stroke is drawn undashed: a hairline, a round-capped line, a butt-capped polyline; a butt-capped line has already become a fill of the line, which covers nothing). Each case is clipped to its own 32x64 cell (a translated group clips in its own space)",
 "width": 128,
 "height": 128,
 "tolerance": {"channel": 8, "pixels": 0},
 "toleranceNote": "Every draw goes through ports of Chrome's own pipeline (Skia's analytic anti-aliasing, edge builder and clipper, stroker and dasher), so what remains is rounding in blending and coverage. 8 leaves room for another Chrome build that rounds differently.",
